From cf00971a8ebbcea1a226cdbcd76c1099ec56801b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:56:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): graphite/warm styles, composer focus halo and
 spring interactions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two more styles, both dark-locked and labelled in all 11 locales:

- `graphite` — the cold-engineering register (Linear / Vercel / x.ai): near-black,
  a single indigo accent, hairline borders, no gradient, no glow anywhere, and
  sharper naive-ui corners (6/4px). Its palette opts out of the focus halo, so
  focusing a field draws a crisp ring instead of a bloom.
- `warm` — the warm-dark register (Warp / OpenCode): warm near-black, warm
  off-white text and no chromatic accent (the primary is paper white, so filled
  buttons read as ink on paper), one warm vignette and slightly translucent
  surfaces so it reads through the cards.

Focus feedback: a new `--input-focus-glow`, derived from each style's own
accent, is prepended to the composer shadow while the field has focus — one
variable covers every style. This also fixes a latent bug where the composer's
focus shadow never showed in dark styles, because `.dark &` set `box-shadow` at
equal specificity but later in the file. naive-ui inputs get the matching
`boxShadowFocus` / `boxShadowActive` ring.

Motion (motion-v 2.4.4, ~46 KB gzip in its own lazily loaded chunk):

- `composables/motion-presets.ts` holds the snappy/soft/gentle springs in one
  place and swaps in a short tween when the OS asks for reduced motion, so that
  switch is honoured centrally instead of per component.
- Tool card: spring expand (replacing the CSS `grid-template-rows` trick), an
  enter reveal, and press feedback on its header.
- Theme / brightness buttons: press feedback.
- Session list: capped nth-child enter stagger in plain CSS — the item root is
  a dynamic `<component :is>` with five call sites, so threading an index prop
  would not have paid for itself.
- Tool panel: spring-shaped `linear()` easing on open/close. It stays a CSS
  transition rather than motion-v because the panel is driven by a Vue
  <Transition> with four lifecycle hooks, and the duration stays 0.25s to match
  the upstream suite.

A spring on `DrawerPanel.vue` was attempted and reverted: that component is dead
code in this fork and is rendered nowhere.
